---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Original PDTF 1.0 standard"
  description="The original PDTF 1.0 JSON standard, its terminology, implementation guidance and adoption evidence."
>
  <PageMeta category="PDTF 1.0" variant="info" updated="Original standard · artefact status varies" />
  <h1>Original PDTF 1.0 standard</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    This is the implementation-facing part of PDTF 1.0: the JSON Schemas and
    overlays, data dictionary, business glossary, implementation guidance and
    adoption evidence associated with the original standard.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">One family, different evidence states</p>
    <p>
      The JSON Schema implementation is the published implementation. Supporting
      terminology, guidance, pilots and evidence keep the status shown on their own
      pages; this category does not promote every record to the same authority.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="use-the-standard">Use and inspect the original standard</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/schema" title="JSON Schemas and overlays" eyebrow="Published implementation" description="Browse the transaction structure, aggregates, overlays and cross-cutting schema views." />
    <GatewayCard href="/modelling/data-dictionary" title="Data dictionary" eyebrow="Source terminology" description="Inspect the schema-derived field catalogue and its recorded definitions." />
    <GatewayCard href="/modelling/business-glossary" title="Business glossary" eyebrow="Source terminology" description="Browse the business concepts and language used by the PDTF 1.0 corpus." />
    <GatewayCard href="/implementation" title="Implementation guidance" eyebrow="For implementers" description="Start quickly, compose schemas, validate transactions and work with verified claims." />
    <GatewayCard href="/adoption" title="Adoption evidence" eyebrow="Evidence" description="Review attributed implementations, pilots and programme evidence without treating it as SPDTF 2.0 adoption." />
  </div>

  <h2 id="relationship">How this relates to the extracted ontology</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/ontology">extracted PDTF 1.0 ontology</a> was
    derived from this schema-led corpus. The original JSON tree remains useful for
    implementation compatibility and traceability, but its nesting does not by itself
    establish the identities and relationships used in future SPDTF 2.0 modelling.
  </p>
</Layout>
